{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_tracing", "label": "Actor tracing", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_receive_span", "label": "actor.receive span", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Opened once per message delivered to onReceive, carrying the actor path and the message type. On error the span records the exception and sets an error status - there is no error.message attribute."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_cluster_envelope_received_span", "label": "cluster.envelope.received span", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The infrastructure span for an inbound cross-cluster envelope carrying a parent trace context, with the sending address and the target path as attributes."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_causal_chaining", "label": "Causal chaining across tells", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "tell snapshots the active span context onto the envelope; on receive the framework runs the handler inside the span so the chain is visible, and application spans appear as children of the auto-generated receive span."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_w3c_traceparent", "label": "W3C traceparent propagation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The same traceparent rides on the wire envelope across cluster nodes; the receiving node extracts it and its receive span links back to the sender."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_all_or_nothing_instrumentation", "label": "All-or-nothing auto-instrumentation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It is active whenever a non-noop tracer is enabled and there are no per-category toggles, so reduce span volume by sampling at the SDK level rather than turning categories off: turning auto-instrumentation off entirely means installing the NoopTracer, which also disables your manual spans since they route through the same tracer."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_span_attributes_exclude_payload", "label": "Span attributes exclude message contents", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The framework includes the message type but never auto-includes message field values, by design - message contents may contain PII or large payloads. Add custom attributes manually where it is safe and useful."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_mdc_trace_id_integration", "label": "Trace IDs are not auto-merged into the MDC", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Log lines are not stamped with the active span IDs out of the box; the MDC fields you set yourself still flow, and copying traceId and spanId from the active span into the log context yourself is what lets you pivot from a slow trace to the matching log lines."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_pipeto_span_gap_actor_tracing", "label": "pipeTo does not propagate the active span", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A known limitation: the target onReceive does not see the caller active span, so capture the carrier manually before piping."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_tracing_cost", "label": "Per-message tracing cost", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Zero overhead with the NoopTracer, since the hot paths short-circuit without allocating spans or doing async-storage lookups. Enabled, each message adds one span allocation, a few attribute writes and one AsyncLocalStorage scope - roughly 5 to 10 microseconds."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_tracing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_receive_span", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/tracing/actor-tracing.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_tracing_actor_tracing_actor_tracing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observab